  "plain": "Scott Ramsay, a researcher of a claimed crash of a craft with alien bodies, talks about a 1950 book called Behind the Flying Saucers, which credited its secret information to a mysterious scientist called Dr. G. Ramsay says his team identified nine scientists behind that name and traced them to the wartime research network of Vannevar Bush, who ran the OSRD, the US office that organised scientific work during the Second World War. He links them to names such as the founders of Texas Instruments, and if true, the crash story would trace back to the core of America's wartime science establishment."
